Subject: Allow native THP decoding to preserve original SDK quarter-IDCT stores
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4

The original RVL THPDec.c quarter-IDCT paths store columns3/4 in the swapped
order already represented by this decoder's disabled compatibility branch.
Expose an opt-in compile definition so the game decoder preserves that retail
quirk. Default Aurora callers retain their current policy. This establishes
that specific store-order boundary, not universal retail video pixel parity.

diff --git a/lib/dolphin/thp/THPDec.cpp b/lib/dolphin/thp/THPDec.cpp
--- a/lib/dolphin/thp/THPDec.cpp
+++ b/lib/dolphin/thp/THPDec.cpp
@@ -35,7 +35,11 @@
 constexpr float kOutputBias = 128.0f * 8.0f;
 
 // Whether to reproduce a bug from SDK THP that swaps columns 3 and 4 in _quarterIDCT
+#if defined(AURORA_THP_PRESERVE_QUARTER_IDCT)
+constexpr bool kBuggyQuarterIdct = AURORA_THP_PRESERVE_QUARTER_IDCT != 0;
+#else
 constexpr bool kBuggyQuarterIdct = false;
+#endif
 
 bool read_segment(aurora::ByteReader& reader, const u8*& data, size_t& size) noexcept {
   u16 encodedSize = 0;
